module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleWire.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingGeometric.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.Colimits
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleRankOneScheme.Basic
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Quasicoherent
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Biproducts
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Untwisting a free presentation: from global generation after a twist to a direct sum of twists

Let `X` be a scheme and `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module. If `F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` is generated by finitely
many global sections, i.e. carries an epimorphism from a finite free module `𝒪_X^{⊕ ι}`, then
tensoring that epimorphism with `L ^⊗ (-n)` presents `F` itself as a quotient of
`⊕_{i ∈ ι} L ^⊗ (-n)`. This is the step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0EBD] that turns clause (7)
of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] into clause (8), and it is the only step of that passage which is *not*
about ampleness: the whole input is the free presentation after the twist.

This file performs that untwisting and nothing else. Ampleness is never mentioned; see the sibling
`Basic.lean` for the clauses of Tag 01Q3 that this serves.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.twistCancelIso`: `(F ⊗ L ^⊗ n) ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n) ≅ F`.
* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule`: **an invertible
  `𝒪_X`-module on a scheme is quasi-coherent.** Absent from both Mathlib and the repository
  before this file; it is what makes the middle term of the dévissage sequence quasi-coherent, and
  hence the kernel too.
* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_biproduct_const`: a finite direct sum of copies of
  a quasi-coherent module is quasi-coherent.
* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.exists_epi_biproduct_of_epi_free`: **the untwisting.** From an
  epimorphism `𝒪_X^{⊕ ι} ⟶ F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` with `ι` finite, an object exhibited as the finite direct
  sum of `ι` copies of `L ^⊗ (-n)` together with an epimorphism from it onto `F`.

## Implementation notes

**Tensoring on the right, not on the left.** The untwisting is `- ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n)` applied to the
presentation. Tensoring on the *right* is used because the cancellation then needs only the
associator and the right unitor:
`(F ⊗ L ^⊗ n) ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n) ≅ F ⊗ (L ^⊗ n ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n)) ≅ F ⊗ 𝟙 ≅ F`, with the middle step
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorPowMulNegIso` at `n` on the nose. The left-hand version
needs the braiding and `tensorPowMulNegIso` at `-n`, hence an `eqToIso` for `-(-n) = n`.

**Why the direct sum is reached through coproducts and only then made a biproduct.** The functor
`tensorRight (L ^⊗ (-n))` is an equivalence (an invertible module's tensor functor is, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_isEquivalence_tensorLeft` transported along
`CategoryTheory.BraidedCategory.tensorLeftIsoTensorRight`), so it preserves colimits of every
size and in particular arbitrary coproducts. It is *also* additive, but
`CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesBiproduct` is only derived from additivity for an index type in
`Type 0` — `CategoryTheory.Functor.PreservesFiniteBiproducts` quantifies over `J : Type` — and the
index type here is the index type of a family of global sections, which lives in the module
universe `u`. Indeed, `CategoryTheory.Functor.mapBiproduct` fails to synthesize
`PreservesBiproduct f T` for `f : ι → X.Modules` with `ι : Type u`. So the transport through the
twist is done with `CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesCoproduct.iso`, which has no such restriction,
and the coproduct is converted to a biproduct at the end by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.biproduct.isoCoproduct`, whose `HasBiproduct` hypothesis comes from
`CategoryTheory.Limits.HasBiproduct.of_hasCoproduct` — universe-polymorphic in the index.

**The three spellings of the category.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules X`,
`SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf` and
`SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf X.presheaf _)` are
  equal by `rfl` but are distinct
terms, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.instCategory` is not the `SheafOfModules` one — its
`Hom` field is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.Hom`. Everything here is therefore stated in
`X.Modules`, with `Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory` and
`Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory` as the local monoidal instances, and the two
places where a `SheafOfModules`-spelled object has to enter carry a declaration pinning its type:
`Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.freeModule` for `SheafOfModules.free` and
`Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.unitModuleIsoUnit` for the identification of `𝒪_X` with the monoidal
unit. Without them the monoidal instance is simply not found, since instance search does not
unfold `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`.

**Quasi-coherence of an invertible module** is obtained through
`Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertibleModule` (clause 1 of
Tag 0B8M on a scheme, unconditional) and the locally free presentation it carries. Mathlib has
`SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsLocallyFree` but no bridge from
`IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank`; the three-line extraction is inlined here because the repository's
only copy of it, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/FibreDimension/ResidueDegreeBound.lean`, is `private`.

No tag attribute is attached: nothing here is the statement of a tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EBD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EBD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory
open Stacks.Ample AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

universe u

namespace Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory

/-- The sheaf condition on the structure presheaf of rings of a scheme, abbreviated: it is the
second argument of every declaration of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/TensorPowers/Basic.lean`
used here. -/
abbrev sheafCondition (X : Scheme.{u}) :=
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X

/-- `𝒪_X` is the monoidal unit of `X.Modules`, with the type of the unit pinned to the
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling of the category. -/
def unitModuleIsoUnit (X : Scheme.{u}) : unitModule X ≅ 𝟙_ X.Modules :=
  Stacks.Ample.unitModuleIsoTensorUnit X

/-- The free `𝒪_X`-module on an index type, with its type pinned to `X.Modules`. Equal to
`SheafOfModules.free` by `rfl`; the pinning is what lets a morphism out of it be composed with a
tensor product. -/
@[ega "0 5.1.1" "O_X^(I) on a scheme"]
def freeModule (X : Scheme.{u}) (ι : Type u) : X.Modules := SheafOfModules.free ι

/-- `freeModule X ι` is the free module `SheafOfModules.free ι`. -/
theorem freeModule_eq (X : Scheme.{u}) (ι : Type u) :
    freeModule X ι = SheafOfModules.free ι := rfl

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **The twist cancels.** `(F ⊗ L ^⊗ n) ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n) ≅ F`, by the associator, the evaluation
isomorphism `L ^⊗ n ⊗ L ^⊗ (-n) ≅ 𝒪_X` of Stacks Tag 01CU and the right unitor. -/
def twistCancelIso (F : X.Modules) (n : ℤ) :
    (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n) ⊗ tensorPowModule X L (-n) ≅ F :=
  α_ F (tensorPowModule X L n) (tensorPowModule X L (-n)) ≪≫
    whiskerLeftIso F (tensorPowMulNegIso X.presheaf (sheafCondition X) L n) ≪≫ ρ_ F

/-- `𝒪_X ⊗ L ^⊗ n ≅ L ^⊗ n`. -/
def unitTensorIso (n : ℤ) :
    unitModule X ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n ≅ tensorPowModule X L n :=
  whiskerRightIso (unitModuleIsoUnit X) _ ≪≫ λ_ _

/-- **Tensoring on the right with a tensor power of an invertible module is an equivalence.**
`tensorLeft` of an invertible module is one by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_isEquivalence_tensorLeft`, and the braiding
identifies the two tensor functors. -/
theorem isEquivalence_tensorRight (n : ℤ) :
    (tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L n)).IsEquivalence :=
  have : (tensorLeft (tensorPowModule X L n)).IsEquivalence :=
    (isInvertible_iff_isEquivalence_tensorLeft X.presheaf (sheafCondition X) _).mp inferInstance
  Functor.isEquivalence_of_iso (BraidedCategory.tensorLeftIsoTensorRight _)

/-- Tensoring on the right with a tensor power of an invertible module preserves colimits of
every size, being an equivalence. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfSize_tensorRight (n : ℤ) :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L n)) :=
  have := isEquivalence_tensorRight L n
  Adjunction.leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
    (tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L n)).asEquivalence.toAdjunction

/-! ### Quasi-coherence -/

/-- **An invertible `𝒪_X`-module on a scheme is quasi-coherent.** By clause 1 of Stacks Tag 0B8M
on a scheme it is finite locally free of rank one, and a locally free presentation is a
quasi-coherent presentation. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule (M : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X M] :
    M.IsQuasicoherent := by
  obtain ⟨q, hfree, -⟩ :=
    (Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertibleModule
      X M).exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData
  let _ : q.IsLocallyFreeData := hfree
  exact q.quasiCoherentData.isQuasicoherent

/-- Every tensor power of an invertible `𝒪_X`-module is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_tensorPowModule (n : ℤ) : (tensorPowModule X L n).IsQuasicoherent :=
  isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertibleModule _

/-- A finite direct sum of copies of a quasi-coherent module is quasi-coherent: the biproduct is
isomorphic to the coproduct, and quasi-coherence is stable under coproducts and isomorphisms. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_biproduct_const {ι : Type u} (M : X.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    [HasBiproduct fun _ : ι => M] : (⨁ fun _ : ι => M).IsQuasicoherent :=
  (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf).prop_of_iso
    (biproduct.isoCoproduct (fun _ : ι => M)).symm
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_sigma (fun _ : ι => M))

/-! ### The untwisting -/

/-- **From a finite free presentation after a positive twist to a quotient of a finite direct sum
of negative twists.** If `F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` receives an epimorphism from the free module on a finite
index type `ι`, then `F` receives one from the direct sum of `ι` copies of `L ^⊗ (-n)`, and that
direct sum is quasi-coherent.

This is the implication (7) ⇒ (8) of Stacks Tag 01Q3 with the ampleness stripped out: nothing is
assumed of `L` beyond invertibility. The direct sum is produced as a bilimit bicone rather than as
`⨁` or `∐`, which is the only form a consumer can apply — see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/HighTwistDevissage/FiniteSum.lean`. -/
theorem exists_epi_biproduct_of_epi_free {ι : Type u} [Finite ι] (n : ℤ) (F : X.Modules)
    (π : freeModule X ι ⟶ F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n) (hπ : Epi π) :
    ∃ (b : Bicone fun _ : ι => tensorPowModule X L (-n)) (_ : b.IsBilimit) (p : b.pt ⟶ F),
      Epi p ∧ b.pt.IsQuasicoherent := by
  have := hπ
  have := isEquivalence_tensorRight L (-n)
  have := preservesColimitsOfSize_tensorRight L (-n)
  have : HasBiproduct (fun _ : ι => tensorPowModule X L (-n)) := HasBiproduct.of_hasCoproduct _
  have := isQuasicoherent_tensorPowModule L (-n)
  refine ⟨biproduct.bicone _, biproduct.isBilimit _,
    (biproduct.isoCoproduct _).hom ≫
      (Sigma.mapIso fun _ : ι => (unitTensorIso L (-n)).symm).hom ≫
      (PreservesCoproduct.iso (tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L (-n)))
        (fun _ : ι => unitModule X)).inv ≫
      (tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L (-n))).map π ≫ (twistCancelIso L F n).hom, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h1 : Epi ((tensorRight (tensorPowModule X L (-n))).map π) := inferInstance
    exact epi_comp' inferInstance (epi_comp' inferInstance
      (epi_comp' inferInstance (epi_comp' h1 inferInstance)))
  · exact isQuasicoherent_biproduct_const _

end Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration

end
